<BaseLayout title="Intake & Air" description="Intake manifolds, throttle body, and IAT placement for LS Gen Coupe swaps.">
  <h1>Intake &amp; Air</h1>
  <p>
    Hood clearance and radiator airflow drive intake choices as much as power goals.
  </p>

  <h2>Manifolds &amp; Throttle Body</h2>
  <p>
    FAST 102 mm and similar fabrications are used; confirm hood clearance with your mounts and engine height.
    Cable vs DBW throttle must match your pedal and ECU strategy (see Accessories and ECU pages).
  </p>

  <h2>IAT Sensor</h2>
  <p>
    Do not leave the IAT where radiator discharge cooks it — readings will be useless.
    Relocating to a tapped port on the manifold (e.g. rear of a FAST 102, ⅜&quot; NPT) is a proven fix.
  </p>

  <h2>Air Filter / Cold Air</h2>
  <p>
    Bay space is limited. Shield the filter from hot radiator air where possible; some builds use custom ducts or relocate the filter toward cooler air at the fender or grille.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
